<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        The general consultation fee.

        The catalogue entry itself is created by 20260924150000_added_phase1_consultation.xml with a
        price of ZERO and a comment saying the fee is a commercial decision rather than something to be
        invented in a migration. That was correct while nobody had supplied a figure. The hospital has
        now given one — KES 1000 — so it is recorded here, in a new changelog rather than by editing
        that one, which is already released and checksummed.

        THREE THINGS WORTH BEING CLEAR ABOUT

        1. This never overwrites a fee that has been set. The UPDATE is guarded on price = 0, so a
           hospital that has already priced its own consultation — through the catalogue screen, or
           /api/hospital-services — keeps that price, and re-running against such a database does
           nothing at all.

        2. This does not freeze the price. The catalogue row remains the single source of truth and an
           administrator may change it at any time; this only fills in the blank that was left.

        3. This is the difference between the real payment path and a placeholder. While the fee was
           zero, every ordinary visit's total came to zero and settled through the "nothing owed" case,
           which deliberately writes no Payment row. From here a normal outpatient visit owes money and
           the cashier flow is exercised for real.

        The INSERT is repeated here as well, so a database where the seed row had somehow been removed
        gets the fee along with it rather than being left with a consultation that cannot be priced.

        Idempotent: both statements are guarded, so re-running is a no-op on a database that already has
        a CONSULTATION entry with a non-zero price.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20260925130000-1" author="hms">
        <comment>Set the general consultation fee to KES 1000 (only where it is still unset)</comment>
        <sql>
            INSERT INTO hospital_service (id, name, service_type, price, active, code)
            SELECT 999001, 'General Consultation', 'CONSULTATION', 1000, true, 'CONSULTATION'
            WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM hospital_service WHERE code = 'CONSULTATION');

            UPDATE hospital_service SET price = 1000 WHERE code = 'CONSULTATION' AND price = 0;
        </sql>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
